---
import Base from "../../layouts/Base.astro";
import Hero from "../../components/Hero.astro";
import EvidenceCarousel from "../../components/EvidenceCarousel.astro";

const evidenceSlides = [
  "Primary care must be the foundation of resilient, high-quality, and efficient health systems.",
  "Health workers need qualified training to practice at the first level of care — community-based health centres and posts.",
  "Family doctors are the medical specialty of primary care.",
  "Trained family doctors identify more conditions, and identify them better, across the full spectrum of health problems.",
  "Family doctors order fewer laboratory and imaging tests — making more rational use of these resources.",
  "Family doctors refer far fewer patients to specialists at the secondary level.",
  "Patients followed by family doctors have substantially lower hospitalization risk across a range of conditions.",
  "Family doctors provide far more consistent follow-up than physicians without this training.",
];
---

<Base
  lang="en"
  title="Adelson G. Jantsch — Family physician and researcher"
  description="Working at the intersection of medical education, implementation research, health-system strengthening, and the smart use of data."
>
  <Hero
    eyebrow="Adelson G. Jantsch · Family Physician & Researcher"
    headlineLine1="Strengthening primary health care and family medicine"
    headlineLine2="in the community, where it happens."
    subline="Working at the intersection of medical education, implementation research, health-system strengthening, and the smart use of data."
    ctaPrimary={{ label: "Explore the impact", href: "/en/impact" }}
    ctaSecondary={{ label: "About me", href: "/en/about" }}
  />
  <EvidenceCarousel
    sectionLabel="EVIDENCE · PRIMARY CARE AND FAMILY MEDICINE"
    slides={evidenceSlides}
    sourceText="Rio de Janeiro cohort · 2010–2018"
    previousLabel="Previous"
    nextLabel="Next"
  />

  <section
    class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 md:px-8 lg:px-12 mt-12 md:mt-16 pb-12 md:pb-16"
  >
    <div
      class="space-y-5 text-base md:text-lg leading-relaxed text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300"
    >
      <p>
        The transition from vertical and selective health systems to a
        comprehensive, effective, and person-centered Primary Health Care
        (PHC) approach remains a critical challenge, especially in low- and
        middle-income countries. Faced with questions regarding the actual
        need for specialized training for medical practice at this level of
        care, this website presents empirical evidence based on cohort
        studies conducted in Rio de Janeiro. The research directly compares
        the performance of general practitioners with that of Family
        Physicians who completed a two-year residency in this specialty,
        analyzing the impact of this specific training on clinical outcomes
        and health system efficiency.
      </p>
      <p>
        The results demonstrate that Family Physicians manage a higher
        volume of chronic conditions per patient and, simultaneously, order
        fewer laboratory and imaging tests compared to general
        practitioners. This specialized training generates measurable
        impacts on increasing pathology detection, optimizing referrals to
        secondary care, reducing hospital admissions, and ensuring
        continuity of care over time. These data are presented here and
        allow you to visualize them dynamically, understand the magnitude
        of the impact that family physicians can make in qualifying patient
        care, and, finally, run population scenario simulations to predict
        the behavior of health expenditures and indicators if general
        practitioners are trained or replaced by specialists.
      </p>
      <p>
        Designed to subsidize structured dialogue, the platform offers
        robust data demonstrating the strategic value of Family Medicine in
        coordinating health systems. This website was created as a tool to
        facilitate dialogue with stakeholders and decision-makers, and to
        support healthcare professionals and researchers in advocating for
        investments in Primary Health Care at local and international
        levels.
      </p>
      <p>
        In addition to sharing information produced in this doctoral
        thesis, I also present the work and projects that I am currently
        conducting in Brazil and other countries.
      </p>
    </div>
    <p
      class="mt-8 text-base md:text-lg font-medium text-accent"
    >
      — Adelson Guaraci Jantsch
    </p>
  </section>
</Base>
